00:43:14.217 --> 00:43:18.618
and he's unloading all
of the raw materials.

00:43:18.618 --> 00:43:19.862
The vegetables and the chicken

00:43:19.862 --> 00:43:20.995
and stuff for Chipotle.
So when you see this,

00:43:20.995 --> 00:43:23.888
just so you know when you
watch this on the show.

00:43:23.888 --> 00:43:27.861
This is probably halfway or
maybe even a little longer

00:43:27.861 --> 00:43:29.919
than halfway through the episode

00:43:29.919 --> 00:43:32.237
when we approach this
guy unloading the stuff

00:43:32.237 --> 00:43:33.663
in the truck behind the Chipotle.

00:43:33.663 --> 00:43:34.715
First thing we shot.
That was literally,

00:43:34.715 --> 00:43:39.132
we were doing our hair and
makeup inside the Chipotle

00:43:41.548 --> 00:43:43.457
that we were shooting at.
Right.

00:43:43.457 --> 00:43:45.564
And then they were like, okay
this is your first scene.

00:43:45.564 --> 00:43:46.823
Because again, everything has to be shot

00:43:46.823 --> 00:43:48.367
according to when things are happening

00:43:48.367 --> 00:43:49.726
and then later it's pieced together

00:43:49.726 --> 00:43:51.936
to make a consistent narrative.

00:43:51.936 --> 00:43:53.973
So yeah us walking around that corner

00:43:53.973 --> 00:43:58.926
making that Law and Order
joke was the very first thing

00:43:58.926 --> 00:44:01.339
we shot with Inside Eats.

00:44:01.339 --> 00:44:02.188
Yeah and we were like,

00:44:02.188 --> 00:44:03.599
"We got a couple of questions for you."

00:44:03.599 --> 00:44:04.482
And he's like, "How are you doing?"

00:44:04.482 --> 00:44:06.505
It's like, "Oh you're gonna
start with the questions."

00:44:06.505 --> 00:44:08.222
And it was all right, we're in the mix.

00:44:08.222 --> 00:44:10.073
Things are, this is happening.

00:44:10.073 --> 00:44:13.017
And we were off to the races.

00:44:13.017 --> 00:44:14.850
It felt, it felt great

00:44:16.418 --> 00:44:19.408
to say at the end of that first day

00:44:19.408 --> 00:44:21.313
or even halfway through the first day

00:44:21.313 --> 00:44:26.124
that my main concern had
been alleviated which was

00:44:26.124 --> 00:44:29.186
are we gonna be in our zone?

00:44:29.186 --> 00:44:31.991
Are we going to be this,

00:44:31.991 --> 00:44:33.162
ourselves.
Ourselves.

00:44:33.162 --> 00:44:36.752
Are we gonna be comfortable, confident

00:44:36.752 --> 00:44:38.669
and having a good time?

00:44:39.624 --> 00:44:43.517
Are we gonna take everything
that we've learned

00:44:43.517 --> 00:44:46.997
from Good Mythical Morning and
even when things would change

00:44:46.997 --> 00:44:48.923
over the years with Good Mythical Morning.

00:44:48.923 --> 00:44:49.961
The bigger the change,

00:44:49.961 --> 00:44:54.961
the more chance that all of a
sudden, our vibe would be off.

00:44:55.280 --> 00:44:56.913
And when everything is new,

00:44:56.913 --> 00:45:00.004
your brain, my brain tends to focus.

00:45:00.004 --> 00:45:04.986
It doesn't yet know what to
tune out and what to focus on.

00:45:04.986 --> 00:45:06.570
Oh there's new people in the crew.

00:45:06.570 --> 00:45:08.899
There's new cameras, it's cold today.

00:45:08.899 --> 00:45:10.219
I'm wearing something different.

00:45:10.219 --> 00:45:11.464
I'm this, that and the other.

00:45:11.464 --> 00:45:12.463
Your back hurts.

00:45:12.463 --> 00:45:13.946
All of these type of variables.

00:45:13.946 --> 00:45:18.941
You have to know what to tune
out and what to focus on.

00:45:18.941 --> 00:45:23.024
To just, to be the most,
to be true to ourselves.

00:45:25.047 --> 00:45:28.760
And just trust our instincts
and be in that moment.

00:45:28.760 --> 00:45:29.790
Well.
And I was very, very happy

00:45:29.790 --> 00:45:32.040
that this show is you know,

00:45:34.200 --> 00:45:35.864
we were never put in a position

00:45:35.864 --> 00:45:39.697
and we never stepped
into a position that was,

00:45:42.129 --> 00:45:46.573
that stretched us in a way
that wasn't a good idea.

00:45:46.573 --> 00:45:47.710
For me, that.

00:45:47.710 --> 00:45:51.053
Just because the people
that we were working with

00:45:51.053 --> 00:45:52.541
had very clearly communicated

00:45:52.541 --> 00:45:56.757
that they understood
what makes us who we are

00:45:56.757 --> 00:45:58.959
and they wanted us to be who we are.

00:45:58.959 --> 00:46:00.205
Yeah.
So I don't think

00:46:00.205 --> 00:46:01.865
I ever felt any.

00:46:01.865 --> 00:46:04.737
There was never a question
in my mind of like,

00:46:04.737 --> 00:46:06.698
are we gonna be put into
the right circumstance

00:46:06.698 --> 00:46:07.571
to pull this off?

00:46:07.571 --> 00:46:10.619
It was more like, you know there's this.

00:46:10.619 --> 00:46:12.387
We are always doing this
little dance you know?

00:46:12.387 --> 00:46:13.783
We had watched.

00:46:13.783 --> 00:46:18.599
The most analogous thing
to this in the recent past

00:46:18.599 --> 00:46:21.499
is The Backup Plan series
that we did on GMN.

00:46:21.499 --> 00:46:23.531
Right.
That was sponsored by Geico.

00:46:23.531 --> 00:46:25.019
Yeah when we went to the cereal factory

00:46:25.019 --> 00:46:26.736
and got in the.
Right.

00:46:26.736 --> 00:46:28.228
So we actually.
The huge cereal bowl

00:46:28.228 --> 00:46:30.354
is a great example.

00:46:30.354 --> 00:46:33.999
We sent those, we sent that
episode of the cereal bowl

00:46:33.999 --> 00:46:36.917
and there was another one where we went to

00:46:36.917 --> 00:46:37.915
oh the.
The flavor.

00:46:37.915 --> 00:46:40.072
The smell, the flavor factory.

00:46:40.072 --> 00:46:44.319
We sent those over to
B17 and TJ and everybody

00:46:44.319 --> 00:46:45.199
and we were like.

00:46:45.199 --> 00:46:47.297
You know we've done this
type of thing before

00:46:47.297 --> 00:46:48.663
and this is sort of the vibe right?

00:46:48.663 --> 00:46:49.835
We're asking a real question

00:46:49.835 --> 00:46:51.797
but we're doing it in a ridiculous way.

00:46:51.797 --> 00:46:53.595
There's gonna be these ridiculous asides

00:46:53.595 --> 00:46:57.157
and we're obviously entering
the situation as a comedy duo.

00:46:57.157 --> 00:46:59.740
I hadn't watched those in years

00:47:00.773 --> 00:47:01.997
and I remember watching them.

00:47:01.997 --> 00:47:03.485
And I remember that night I watched them

00:47:03.485 --> 00:47:05.776
and immediately sent those
two episodes to you and Stevie

00:47:05.776 --> 00:47:08.329
'cause I was like hey, I didn't
know how I was gonna feel.

00:47:08.329 --> 00:47:09.874
You never know how you're
gonna feel about something

00:47:09.874 --> 00:47:11.414
when you go back to it years later.

00:47:11.414 --> 00:47:12.301
Yeah.
'Cause you always feel like

00:47:12.301 --> 00:47:14.736
you've developed beyond it or whatever.

00:47:14.736 --> 00:47:15.752
Yeah.
I was like hey, this is the.

00:47:15.752 --> 00:47:17.665
This is the true north.

00:47:17.665 --> 00:47:20.602
The way that we interacted here.

00:47:20.602 --> 00:47:22.507
This is how we.

00:47:22.507 --> 00:47:25.078
This is the vibe that
we should attain right?

00:47:25.078 --> 00:47:26.586
This is the vibe we should go for.

00:47:26.586 --> 00:47:27.925
Yeah.

00:47:27.925 --> 00:47:30.323
And I think we really got there.

00:47:30.323 --> 00:47:32.822
I mean there's always a little bit,

00:47:32.822 --> 00:47:35.189
it depends on what
we're doing at the time.

00:47:35.189 --> 00:47:38.373
There are moments in this type of format

00:47:38.373 --> 00:47:40.711
where we get to a place where me and you

00:47:40.711 --> 00:47:43.045
are standing there talking to one person

00:47:43.045 --> 00:47:46.754
and asking them questions
and not doing something.

00:47:46.754 --> 00:47:50.250
And it gets to be like two
guys interviewing two person

00:47:50.250 --> 00:47:52.071
and since nothing is scripted.

00:47:52.071 --> 00:47:54.470
Again like yes we had this notebook

00:47:54.470 --> 00:47:56.781
that's like here's some
questions you could ask.

00:47:56.781 --> 00:47:58.884
Here's what this person knows.

00:47:58.884 --> 00:48:00.839
Here is the goal of this scene.

00:48:00.839 --> 00:48:04.095
We had all kind of developed
that and then Nick and TJ

00:48:04.095 --> 00:48:05.761
had put it in this big
binder that we were given

00:48:05.761 --> 00:48:07.197
when we got on set so
we reorient ourselves

00:48:07.197 --> 00:48:09.469
but when the camera starts rolling,

00:48:09.469 --> 00:48:12.253
you don't remember what the binder said.

00:48:12.253 --> 00:48:13.843
You remember bits and pieces of it

00:48:13.843 --> 00:48:15.470
but you're really going on instinct.

00:48:15.470 --> 00:48:17.123
Yeah.
And so you've got

00:48:17.123 --> 00:48:18.069
what you're thinking.

00:48:18.069 --> 00:48:20.190
I've got what I'm thinking.

00:48:20.190 --> 00:48:21.470
Oh, Link just said that.

00:48:21.470 --> 00:48:24.150
I'm gonna go with that or
that makes me think this.

00:48:24.150 --> 00:48:26.666
I'm gonna get out of his way for a second.

00:48:26.666 --> 00:48:28.249
There is this debt.

00:48:29.725 --> 00:48:32.420
There's a balance in trying to
figure out that dance again.

00:48:32.420 --> 00:48:34.209
Yeah the brain gets hot.

00:48:34.209 --> 00:48:35.083
There's a lot going on.

00:48:35.083 --> 00:48:39.390
But it pretty much came back immediately.

00:48:39.390 --> 00:48:41.630
It wasn't like a struggle.
Yeah, very glad about that.

00:48:41.630 --> 00:48:42.661
So I think you know,

00:48:42.661 --> 00:48:47.441
so when we were bringing
our comedic sensibility

00:48:47.441 --> 00:48:51.972
and our curiosity to the
table and to every scene,

00:48:51.972 --> 00:48:55.608
having structured the episodes
and gotten approval on that.

00:48:55.608 --> 00:48:59.805
The thing that Food
Network was bringing to us

00:48:59.805 --> 00:49:03.608
was an education on their
expectations from their audience

00:49:03.608 --> 00:49:08.439
'cause this is a melding
of two audiences you know?

00:49:08.439 --> 00:49:12.325
Between a Food Network,
Discovery+ and Mythical Beasts.

00:49:12.325 --> 00:49:13.212
And I would

00:49:13.212 --> 00:49:14.139
say specifically.
And I would like

00:49:14.139 --> 00:49:14.993
to talk about that.
I would say

00:49:14.993 --> 00:49:17.152
specifically Food Network which yes,

00:49:17.152 --> 00:49:18.339
Food Network is a part of Discovery

00:49:18.339 --> 00:49:22.672
but when we got approached,
we actually didn't know.

00:49:25.678 --> 00:49:29.071
I don't know if I missed
it or if it developed later

00:49:29.071 --> 00:49:30.957
but we didn't know that it
was a Food Network show.

00:49:30.957 --> 00:49:33.527
The conversation was Discovery+.

00:49:33.527 --> 00:49:35.321
Right.
So,

00:49:35.321 --> 00:49:38.235
I knew it was gonna be food-centric

00:49:38.235 --> 00:49:40.200
because that's the whole point of the show

00:49:40.200 --> 00:49:42.981
but the moment that it either became

00:49:42.981 --> 00:49:44.186
or I finally realized.
We didn't know if it

00:49:44.186 --> 00:49:46.578
would be comedy-centric with food

00:49:46.578 --> 00:49:49.077
but it became.
Well there's a, yeah.

00:49:49.077 --> 00:49:52.338
Clear that it needed to be food-centric.

00:49:52.338 --> 00:49:56.829
Right, and when we say
food-centric, what we mean is that.

00:49:56.829 --> 00:49:59.444
So a person who has decided
to turn on Food Network

00:49:59.444 --> 00:50:01.470
and maybe you're one of those people.

00:50:01.470 --> 00:50:03.014
If you're like me,

00:50:03.014 --> 00:50:05.355
you're just the kind of
person that just likes

00:50:05.355 --> 00:50:07.484
to look at food right?

00:50:07.484 --> 00:50:10.171
You like to look at food
and see people make food

00:50:10.171 --> 00:50:11.640
and see people eat food

00:50:11.640 --> 00:50:15.170
because you have a love affair with food.

00:50:15.170 --> 00:50:18.430
It's probably the best thing on earth

00:50:18.430 --> 00:50:21.255
besides what rhymes with Tussy.

00:50:21.255 --> 00:50:22.240
Okay.
That we talked

00:50:22.240 --> 00:50:23.145
about earlier.

00:50:23.145 --> 00:50:26.228
And so people who watch Food Network,

00:50:28.619 --> 00:50:30.667
they need to see food.

00:50:30.667 --> 00:50:34.828
Right, they don't just want
to see two guys being stupid,

00:50:34.828 --> 00:50:36.000
being funny.
Yeah.

00:50:36.000 --> 00:50:39.036
Because if you're a Food Network first,

00:50:39.036 --> 00:50:40.948
if you're tuning in for Food Network first

00:50:40.948 --> 00:50:42.353
and not Rhett and Link first.

00:50:42.353 --> 00:50:45.248
You're like I'm here for the
food part of the network.

00:50:45.248 --> 00:50:49.208
I don't want these two guys
to get in the way of the food.

00:50:49.208 --> 00:50:51.208
And so there was one guy

00:50:53.002 --> 00:50:55.438
who had a sort of specialized camera.

00:50:55.438 --> 00:50:56.392
It was a different camera

00:50:56.392 --> 00:50:59.180
that could do a really high
frame rate for slow motion.

00:50:59.180 --> 00:51:01.763
And he was the food camera guy.

00:51:05.368 --> 00:51:07.426
Yeah.
And so if the guacamole

00:51:07.426 --> 00:51:10.698
is being made or dipped out of something

00:51:10.698 --> 00:51:13.313
or steak is being chopped,

00:51:13.313 --> 00:51:15.816
it's being like that's when
those sort of hero shots

00:51:15.816 --> 00:51:17.213
or whatever you want to call them,

00:51:17.213 --> 00:51:19.140
slow-mo, sort of dramatic food shots.

00:51:19.140 --> 00:51:20.727
He was getting all,

00:51:20.727 --> 00:51:23.248
and as he was getting all this footage.

00:51:23.248 --> 00:51:25.967
Me, not really understanding the show

00:51:25.967 --> 00:51:27.927
that we were making yet, I was like,

00:51:27.927 --> 00:51:30.678
"Wow, he's filming a lot,
he's filming all this food.

00:51:30.678 --> 00:51:33.924
"But I mean it's gonna
be us on camera right?"

00:51:33.924 --> 00:51:35.434
You know it was like,

00:51:35.434 --> 00:51:37.362
I mean if we're gonna be the
funny guys on camera right.

00:51:37.362 --> 00:51:41.646
So there was a realignment that happened

00:51:41.646 --> 00:51:45.261
in terms of like understanding the,

00:51:45.261 --> 00:51:47.205
where everything should settle.

00:51:47.205 --> 00:51:50.538
What the balance should be for this show

00:51:51.505 --> 00:51:53.182
and really begin to understand

00:51:53.182 --> 00:51:57.194
and getting that Food
Network education that hey,

00:51:57.194 --> 00:52:01.212
the audience wants to
indulge with their eyes.

00:52:01.212 --> 00:52:02.581
You know?

00:52:02.581 --> 00:52:03.479
And you can,

00:52:03.479 --> 00:52:04.913
yeah we can have fun all along the way.

00:52:04.913 --> 00:52:08.124
But you want to indulge
and you want to learn.

00:52:08.124 --> 00:52:11.003
So as we were in the post-phase

00:52:11.003 --> 00:52:13.642
of editing everything together

00:52:13.642 --> 00:52:17.012
and we were giving a bunch of
notes about like all right,

00:52:17.012 --> 00:52:20.198
I remember saying this
and we had, it was funny.

00:52:20.198 --> 00:52:21.676
Or I remember Rhett said this,

00:52:21.676 --> 00:52:23.693
they're like there's
three things from Rhett.

00:52:23.693 --> 00:52:24.900
There's nothing from me.

00:52:24.900 --> 00:52:27.564
Let's have a little bit
more balance or vice versa.

00:52:27.564 --> 00:52:29.273
We would give these type of notes.

00:52:29.273 --> 00:52:30.516
Right.
Or this is a runner.

00:52:30.516 --> 00:52:32.530
I think we have a throwback.

00:52:32.530 --> 00:52:34.382
You know comedy notes.

00:52:34.382 --> 00:52:37.010
Yeah the thing that we're interested in.

00:52:37.010 --> 00:52:38.938
And the Food Network notes would be like,

00:52:38.938 --> 00:52:41.654
we need to understand more of the process.

00:52:41.654 --> 00:52:43.529
You started making the guacamole

00:52:43.529 --> 00:52:45.688
but we don't know what the final,

00:52:45.688 --> 00:52:48.781
you didn't reveal what
the final ingredient was.

00:52:48.781 --> 00:52:50.186
It didn't come together.

00:52:50.186 --> 00:52:51.539
It's like you gotta have.

00:52:51.539 --> 00:52:55.531
If you're gonna go into
this guacamole moment,

00:52:55.531 --> 00:52:57.406
well it needs to have a
beginning, middle and end.

00:52:57.406 --> 00:52:59.460
You gotta have a satisfying conclusion

00:52:59.460 --> 00:53:00.536
so that people feel like

00:53:00.536 --> 00:53:03.484
they've got the full guac experience

00:53:03.484 --> 00:53:05.055
and it totally makes sense.
And you want to,

00:53:05.055 --> 00:53:06.440
and you want to see the guac

00:53:06.440 --> 00:53:09.177
and hey if there's a fact
about how many avocados

00:53:09.177 --> 00:53:12.594
Chipotle goes through in a year or a week

00:53:13.858 --> 00:53:14.954
or whatever that fact was.

00:53:14.954 --> 00:53:16.826
That's an interesting thing.

00:53:16.826 --> 00:53:20.261
We didn't ask that in scene
but we can pull a voiceover.

00:53:20.261 --> 00:53:21.738
We can change that.

00:53:21.738 --> 00:53:24.657
And whenever you start
to learn these things,

00:53:24.657 --> 00:53:26.961
well now let's add another layer

00:53:26.961 --> 00:53:29.711
where we're doing some animations

00:53:30.942 --> 00:53:33.858
that illustrate the things
that you're learning

00:53:33.858 --> 00:53:35.744
from a culinary standpoint.

00:53:35.744 --> 00:53:37.395
And I think the point.
And so that was added

00:53:37.395 --> 00:53:38.371
to the show.

00:53:38.371 --> 00:53:39.688
I think the point of this,

00:53:39.688 --> 00:53:43.052
like what I am hoping that you listening

00:53:43.052 --> 00:53:46.635
will take from this
discussion is you know,

00:53:48.455 --> 00:53:51.955
if we made this show and we were making it

00:53:53.884 --> 00:53:56.284
for the Good Mythical Morning audience.

00:53:56.284 --> 00:53:58.716
Right.
We were going into Chipotle

00:53:58.716 --> 00:54:02.315
and asking this question
and then putting it on

00:54:02.315 --> 00:54:04.892
to an episode of GMM
or as an episode of GMM

00:54:04.892 --> 00:54:06.361
like we do with The Backup Plan.

00:54:06.361 --> 00:54:09.691
Because you're tuning in
to Good Mythical Morning

00:54:09.691 --> 00:54:12.791
we think primarily to hang out with us,

00:54:12.791 --> 00:54:16.537
then it's gonna be almost like 90 to 95%

00:54:16.537 --> 00:54:20.704
just us being us and using
this canvas of Chipotle

00:54:21.735 --> 00:54:24.072
as an opportunity to be funny right?

00:54:24.072 --> 00:54:25.912
Yeah.
But because

00:54:25.912 --> 00:54:28.606
the intended audience
is first and foremost

00:54:28.606 --> 00:54:31.296
is someone who's interested
in food television,

00:54:31.296 --> 00:54:32.952
Food Network.

00:54:32.952 --> 00:54:34.807
It is a food show first

00:54:34.807 --> 00:54:36.693
that we are then bringing all that

00:54:36.693 --> 00:54:40.185
Rhett and Link ridiculousness
and curiosity into.

00:54:40.185 --> 00:54:43.443
To kind of create more of a balance.

00:54:43.443 --> 00:54:46.810
So while I do think it is the most,

00:54:46.810 --> 00:54:49.364
I don't wanna say it's the
funniest show on Food Network.

00:54:49.364 --> 00:54:51.185
I mean I think Guy Fieri is very funny

00:54:51.185 --> 00:54:55.352
but I think it the most
intentionally comedic show

00:54:56.582 --> 00:54:58.186
on Food Network.

00:54:58.186 --> 00:54:59.680
And shout out to Alton Brown

00:54:59.680 --> 00:55:01.673
who we still want to have on GMM.

00:55:01.673 --> 00:55:02.576
Yeah yeah yeah.

00:55:02.576 --> 00:55:06.629
You know he did more
like this sketch thing

00:55:06.629 --> 00:55:09.058
at the top of his show.

00:55:09.058 --> 00:55:11.650
Well one of his shows and you know,

00:55:11.650 --> 00:55:14.711
that's another thing that we did succeed

00:55:14.711 --> 00:55:16.205
at starting with comedy.

00:55:16.205 --> 00:55:17.281
Like there's basically

00:55:17.281 --> 00:55:18.907
a sketch.
Well let me clarify

00:55:18.907 --> 00:55:19.805
real quick.

00:55:19.805 --> 00:55:21.299
I just made it sound like I was saying

00:55:21.299 --> 00:55:23.353
that Guy Fieri is unintentionally funny.

00:55:23.353 --> 00:55:25.061
No, I'm just saying that like,

00:55:25.061 --> 00:55:28.211
he's coming in there first
and foremost as a chef

00:55:28.211 --> 00:55:29.831
who happens to be very funny.

00:55:29.831 --> 00:55:31.700
We're coming in as comedians

00:55:31.700 --> 00:55:33.536
who just happen to some knowledge about,

00:55:33.536 --> 00:55:34.925
experience with food.
Oh I got you.

00:55:34.925 --> 00:55:35.985
You know what I'm saying?

00:55:35.985 --> 00:55:37.621
I got you.

00:55:37.621 --> 00:55:40.470
But yeah, I am curious at this.

00:55:40.470 --> 00:55:42.586
You know we're talking to you

00:55:42.586 --> 00:55:44.600
and kind of telling you
what our perspective is.

00:55:44.600 --> 00:55:47.059
And all of this I think has come together

00:55:47.059 --> 00:55:49.151
in a show that makes the most sense.

00:55:49.151 --> 00:55:53.385
That is satisfying on all
of these levels you know?

00:55:53.385 --> 00:55:56.492
Are there as many jokes as we made?

00:55:56.492 --> 00:55:57.551
Of course not.

00:55:57.551 --> 00:55:58.768
There's lots of stuff that got cut.

00:55:58.768 --> 00:56:00.767
But there are more just so you know.

00:56:00.767 --> 00:56:03.796
Again, when you're doing linear television

00:56:03.796 --> 00:56:05.358
that's actually gonna
show up on Food Network

00:56:05.358 --> 00:56:07.281
and have commercial breaks.

00:56:07.281 --> 00:56:10.905
That episode is about 22
minutes of content right?

00:56:10.905 --> 00:56:12.402
That's how much content ends up being

00:56:12.402 --> 00:56:14.717
in a half hour block of
traditional television.

00:56:14.717 --> 00:56:16.237
So you've gotta hit 22 minutes.

00:56:16.237 --> 00:56:19.140
Obviously on Discovery+,
streaming service,

00:56:19.140 --> 00:56:20.266
you don't have to hit that.

00:56:20.266 --> 00:56:22.971
So we had these additional,

00:56:22.971 --> 00:56:25.376
sometimes a completely new scene

00:56:25.376 --> 00:56:28.017
and sometimes just a new
thing that happened in a scene

00:56:28.017 --> 00:56:30.295
and all those have been added in

00:56:30.295 --> 00:56:31.278
when you watch it on Discovery+.

00:56:31.278 --> 00:56:35.935
So you might get like a 25, 26
minute episode on Discovery+

00:56:35.935 --> 00:56:38.597
and most of that's gonna be stuff

00:56:38.597 --> 00:56:40.895
that wasn't essential

00:56:40.895 --> 00:56:43.684
or integral to a Food Network audience.

00:56:43.684 --> 00:56:48.444
So it tends to be some of
the funny tangential stuff

00:56:48.444 --> 00:56:50.071
that happened in the moment.

00:56:50.071 --> 00:56:52.451
The thing that I'm most
interested in at this point,

00:56:52.451 --> 00:56:56.727
because it hasn't premiered
yet as of this recording.

00:56:56.727 --> 00:57:00.563
Is yeah, what is the reception gonna be?

00:57:00.563 --> 00:57:04.333
What, what are Mythical
Beasts going to think of it?

00:57:04.333 --> 00:57:06.718
What is the Food Network
audience gonna think?

00:57:06.718 --> 00:57:08.366
How are we going to find out

00:57:08.366 --> 00:57:11.662
what non Mythical Beasts think?

00:57:11.662 --> 00:57:12.624
Oh.
We are gonna get

00:57:12.624 --> 00:57:13.547
that feedback?

00:57:13.547 --> 00:57:16.211
I'm sure we'll find that out.

00:57:16.211 --> 00:57:17.044
You know?

00:57:17.044 --> 00:57:18.079
It's like we'll have
to go to other places,

00:57:18.079 --> 00:57:21.134
other ways that the show is posted online.

00:57:21.134 --> 00:57:24.757
Or promos of it are posted online.

00:57:24.757 --> 00:57:28.201
Just to you know, tap into
that buzz but I'm just,

00:57:28.201 --> 00:57:31.013
I'm interested because again,

00:57:31.013 --> 00:57:33.576
it's like every time you put something out

00:57:33.576 --> 00:57:36.691
for a new type of audience it's like,

00:57:36.691 --> 00:57:39.209
well are they gonna
hate one or both of us?

00:57:39.209 --> 00:57:40.503
Well there's.
And I just know,

00:57:40.503 --> 00:57:44.777
you know I just, I know that
with the way that I do things.

00:57:44.777 --> 00:57:47.527
It's like, I'm not for everybody.

00:57:49.470 --> 00:57:50.490
I'm not for everybody.

00:57:50.490 --> 00:57:52.226
So I'm kind of prepared for that.

00:57:52.226 --> 00:57:53.951
It's like, and I.

00:57:53.951 --> 00:57:56.246
But I don't, and if that's the reason

00:57:56.246 --> 00:57:58.040
the show doesn't work, so be it.

00:57:58.040 --> 00:57:59.318
Well I could.
The show ain't gonna

00:57:59.318 --> 00:58:00.241
work without me.

00:58:00.241 --> 00:58:01.165
I'll just have to do season two alone.

00:58:01.165 --> 00:58:02.298
Well this is your -
Or maybe I oughta do it

00:58:02.298 --> 00:58:03.222
with DJ Rhett.

00:58:03.222 --> 00:58:04.752
No this is your opportunity to say,

00:58:04.752 --> 00:58:06.733
people don't like me either.

00:58:06.733 --> 00:58:08.491
That's true, a lot of
people don't like me.

00:58:08.491 --> 00:58:10.712
Maybe more people than don't like you.

00:58:10.712 --> 00:58:12.339
Right.
But so there's a question

00:58:12.339 --> 00:58:17.109
of like is the traditional
Food Network audience

00:58:17.109 --> 00:58:18.058
going to be like,

00:58:18.058 --> 00:58:21.000
"I want to see somebody
who's making great food.

00:58:21.000 --> 00:58:21.999
"I don't want to see a couple of idiots

00:58:21.999 --> 00:58:23.965
"who are just having fun with food."?

00:58:23.965 --> 00:58:27.434
And then on the opposite
end of the spectrum,

00:58:27.434 --> 00:58:28.359
are there people who are like,

00:58:28.359 --> 00:58:29.527
"I'm just coming here
for the ridiculousness

00:58:29.527 --> 00:58:30.526
"of Rhett and Link

00:58:30.526 --> 00:58:32.819
"and I don't care about
all the food shots."?

00:58:32.819 --> 00:58:34.521
Because we have made a show

00:58:34.521 --> 00:58:38.445
that is a compromise between
what both parties want.

00:58:38.445 --> 00:58:40.993
I believe that, I mean for me,

00:58:40.993 --> 00:58:43.456
because I do like food a lot

00:58:43.456 --> 00:58:45.990
and I like food facts and
I like to see the process.

00:58:45.990 --> 00:58:47.211
It was fascinating to get to know

00:58:47.211 --> 00:58:50.886
the people who are making the decisions

00:58:50.886 --> 00:58:52.789
about what ends up on the Chipotle menu

00:58:52.789 --> 00:58:54.232
or The Cheesecake Factory menu.

00:58:54.232 --> 00:58:56.853
The people behind these
incredible flavors at Coolhaus.

00:58:56.853 --> 00:59:00.117
The scientists, the flavor scientists

00:59:00.117 --> 00:59:02.318
behind Beyond Meat.
Yeah.

00:59:02.318 --> 00:59:04.203
That's all super fascinating stuff to me.

00:59:04.203 --> 00:59:07.437
That's personally more
fascinating than me making a joke.

00:59:07.437 --> 00:59:10.937
So I feel like it landed in a great place.

00:59:12.639 --> 00:59:13.568
I do too.

00:59:13.568 --> 00:59:15.876
I'm very proud of this show.

00:59:15.876 --> 00:59:18.024
I was very proud of Commercial Kings

00:59:18.024 --> 00:59:20.038
and if we had the opportunity.

00:59:20.038 --> 00:59:21.670
If they had ordered more,

00:59:21.670 --> 00:59:23.426
we would've turned a corner

00:59:23.426 --> 00:59:25.998
and it would've gotten that much better.

00:59:25.998 --> 00:59:30.998
But the core of that show was
something I'm very proud of

00:59:31.142 --> 00:59:32.581
and I wish they would've ordered more.

00:59:32.581 --> 00:59:33.897
I'm glad that they didn't

00:59:33.897 --> 00:59:36.632
because Good Mythical Morning
may have never existed

00:59:36.632 --> 00:59:39.336
and we wouldn't be here today.

00:59:39.336 --> 00:59:42.832
But we learned so much
in these four episodes.

00:59:42.832 --> 00:59:44.738
Yeah.
Of figuring out

00:59:44.738 --> 00:59:49.453
what the show is and how
to ask those questions

00:59:49.453 --> 00:59:51.472
and what we should actually be shooting

00:59:51.472 --> 00:59:53.249
and the things that we
should actually be doing

00:59:53.249 --> 00:59:55.243
that I feel like,

00:59:55.243 --> 00:59:58.814
I'm not saying there's.
We have so much more focus.

00:59:58.814 --> 01:00:00.207
I'm not saying there's anything,

01:00:00.207 --> 01:00:01.700
I think where we ended up with season one

01:00:01.700 --> 01:00:04.090
after a lot of edits and
a lot of back and forth

01:00:04.090 --> 01:00:05.014
and figuring that out.

01:00:05.014 --> 01:00:08.838
We kind of know exactly what the mode is

01:00:08.838 --> 01:00:10.384
and what the final
project is gonna be going,

01:00:10.384 --> 01:00:12.450
if we can go into a second season.

01:00:12.450 --> 01:00:14.470
Where I would just be
that much more confident

01:00:14.470 --> 01:00:15.871
to make a great television show.

01:00:15.871 --> 01:00:19.539
But we've experienced
enough to know that like,

01:00:19.539 --> 01:00:20.646
you know it could go either way.

01:00:20.646 --> 01:00:21.632
We're very hopeful.

01:00:21.632 --> 01:00:24.485
We believe that this show has legs

01:00:24.485 --> 01:00:26.650
and we want to keep making it.

01:00:26.650 --> 01:00:29.100
But you know, there's so many factors.

01:00:29.100 --> 01:00:31.036
Yeah.
Not the least of which is

01:00:31.036 --> 01:00:33.126
who, again at this point,

01:00:33.126 --> 01:00:36.127
who knows how it will be interpreted?

01:00:36.127 --> 01:00:37.935
How we will be interpreted

01:00:37.935 --> 01:00:40.935
within the Food Network programming.

01:00:41.874 --> 01:00:43.266
Yeah.
That's just very,

01:00:43.266 --> 01:00:46.139
'cause it is, it is a
different type of show

01:00:46.139 --> 01:00:51.058
that pushes the comedy more
and it is, it's unique.

01:00:51.058 --> 01:00:56.058
So that's a good thing if
enough people are ready for it.

01:00:56.380 --> 01:00:59.932
If they have, pun intended,
an appetite for it.

01:00:59.932 --> 01:01:02.265
Now I haven't really come,

01:01:03.428 --> 01:01:05.783
I haven't made a definitive
decision about this

01:01:05.783 --> 01:01:10.204
but I am considering and
strongly leaning toward

01:01:10.204 --> 01:01:13.708
not reading anything about the show.

01:01:13.708 --> 01:01:17.950
Not looking at anyone's
thoughts about the show.

01:01:17.950 --> 01:01:20.391
We've never done that
with anything we've made.

01:01:20.391 --> 01:01:22.478
Why would you start now?

01:01:22.478 --> 01:01:23.871
I'm getting much more.

01:01:23.871 --> 01:01:27.825
Actually, I am moving in that
direction much, much more.

01:01:27.825 --> 01:01:30.026
I find it to be a much healthier place.

01:01:30.026 --> 01:01:32.609
Because while the vast majority

01:01:33.522 --> 01:01:34.493
of the feedback that we get

01:01:34.493 --> 01:01:36.754
on the things that we do is positive

01:01:36.754 --> 01:01:38.711
because we've got such
a supportive fanbase.

01:01:38.711 --> 01:01:42.869
First of all you know
that the minority comments

01:01:42.869 --> 01:01:44.711
who are gonna say something hurtful,

01:01:44.711 --> 01:01:46.614
those are the ones that you remember.

01:01:46.614 --> 01:01:50.700
But also I find myself not
being in a healthy place

01:01:50.700 --> 01:01:53.739
when I'm trying to find
the positive comments.

01:01:53.739 --> 01:01:55.581
Yeah.
To outweigh

01:01:55.581 --> 01:01:57.445
the negative comments and then I realize

01:01:57.445 --> 01:02:00.023
that I am finding my identity and my value

01:02:00.023 --> 01:02:02.419
in other people's
interpretation of my work.

01:02:02.419 --> 01:02:04.873
Where what I'm trying
to do is get to a place

01:02:04.873 --> 01:02:08.998
where I am happy with
what this ended up being

01:02:08.998 --> 01:02:11.233
and so that's the only
thing that I need to know.

01:02:11.233 --> 01:02:12.892
Is that I am proud of it.

01:02:12.892 --> 01:02:15.718
I know what I like about it,
what I don't like about it.

01:02:15.718 --> 01:02:18.851
My thoughts about it, what
I would do differently.

01:02:18.851 --> 01:02:22.434
Now we have people who
are here at Mythical

01:02:23.397 --> 01:02:28.164
who are going to tell us the
aggregate opinions of people

01:02:28.164 --> 01:02:29.783
which are very helpful.

01:02:29.783 --> 01:02:30.744
I'm not saying

01:02:30.744 --> 01:02:34.096
I don't want to take the
audience's reception into account

01:02:34.096 --> 01:02:37.000
because you're not a good
producer if you don't do that.

01:02:37.000 --> 01:02:38.424
If you don't know what
the audience thinks.

01:02:38.424 --> 01:02:41.673
But there is something
that happens emotionally

01:02:41.673 --> 01:02:44.905
and mentally when you interact directly

01:02:44.905 --> 01:02:47.359
with either a compliment or a criticism.

01:02:47.359 --> 01:02:51.914
That I don't think is
necessarily good for my psyche.

01:02:51.914 --> 01:02:53.831
Well, I applaud that.

01:02:55.278 --> 01:02:58.052
I actually think talking
out both sides of my mouth

01:02:58.052 --> 01:02:59.861
'cause I said that we've
never done that before

01:02:59.861 --> 01:03:01.890
but the more I think about it,

01:03:01.890 --> 01:03:04.648
I read stuff less and less.

01:03:04.648 --> 01:03:07.231
Like I'm kind of a, what's the?

01:03:09.718 --> 01:03:11.866
I'm a hermit in.

01:03:11.866 --> 01:03:14.979
I'm like a social media hermit.

01:03:14.979 --> 01:03:18.633
I mean, you tell me lots of
things that I don't read.

01:03:18.633 --> 01:03:21.081
That they never crossed my path.

01:03:21.081 --> 01:03:22.504
Yeah.
So actually,

01:03:22.504 --> 01:03:24.115
you're a lot more prone to it than I am.

01:03:24.115 --> 01:03:27.488
I think I'll probably end up
just being like, you know.

01:03:27.488 --> 01:03:30.222
I didn't end up reading anything.

01:03:30.222 --> 01:03:31.536
Well it's things like.
But a new project is.

01:03:31.536 --> 01:03:33.837
I can be having a good.
Your friend

01:03:33.837 --> 01:03:35.427
and like the ongoing stuff.

01:03:35.427 --> 01:03:37.280
I can be having a good day

01:03:37.280 --> 01:03:41.947
and then I make the horrible
decision to go and look at,

01:03:44.394 --> 01:03:46.590
I mean I haven't done this recently.

01:03:46.590 --> 01:03:49.935
I'm just saying back when it
was a relevant thing to do.

01:03:49.935 --> 01:03:52.918
Look at the Goodreads reviews for

01:03:52.918 --> 01:03:54.186
"The Lost Causes of Bleak Creek".

01:03:54.186 --> 01:03:55.607
Now first of all, again.

01:03:55.607 --> 01:03:58.533
The aggregate of that book

01:03:58.533 --> 01:04:00.248
and the rating is very high right?

01:04:00.248 --> 01:04:02.415
I'm proud of that book.

01:04:02.415 --> 01:04:03.898
Obviously we're not novelists

01:04:03.898 --> 01:04:05.885
and I didn't think it was gonna be,

01:04:05.885 --> 01:04:07.113
like win the Pulitzer Prize

01:04:07.113 --> 01:04:08.811
and we learned a lot in doing it.

01:04:08.811 --> 01:04:12.926
But I'm proud of what it
ended up being for what it is.

01:04:12.926 --> 01:04:16.347
But there are people who come to Goodreads

01:04:16.347 --> 01:04:18.513
who see themselves as literary critics

01:04:18.513 --> 01:04:21.607
and then just write these scathing reviews

01:04:21.607 --> 01:04:22.606
and some of them you're like,

01:04:22.606 --> 01:04:23.772
"Well yeah that's true."

01:04:23.772 --> 01:04:25.252
Or yeah, you're right about that.

01:04:25.252 --> 01:04:26.790
That puts me in,

01:04:26.790 --> 01:04:30.749
but I already know what I
think about that process.

01:04:30.749 --> 01:04:32.810
I already know how I feel about that book.

01:04:32.810 --> 01:04:35.329
I already know how I feel about
what we would do differently

01:04:35.329 --> 01:04:37.789
if we were to do a
second one in the series

01:04:37.789 --> 01:04:38.789
or whatever.
Yep.

01:04:38.789 --> 01:04:40.188
So you're not learning anything.

01:04:40.188 --> 01:04:43.088
I'm only suffering emotionally.

01:04:43.088 --> 01:04:46.278
So as I try to release myself

01:04:46.278 --> 01:04:47.563
from things that I can't control

01:04:47.563 --> 01:04:49.895
which is people's opinions about our work,

01:04:49.895 --> 01:04:53.687
what I can't control is our work right?

01:04:53.687 --> 01:04:55.923
I have an opinion about it

01:04:55.923 --> 01:04:57.649
and that opinion can be incorporated

01:04:57.649 --> 01:04:59.149
into the next iteration

01:04:59.149 --> 01:05:00.728
and it just feels like
a much healthier place.

01:05:00.728 --> 01:05:02.658
So because of all the things

01:05:02.658 --> 01:05:03.854
that you were just saying about,

01:05:03.854 --> 01:05:08.023
yes there's gonna be people
who are like, actively,

01:05:08.023 --> 01:05:10.690
I don't want this on my network.

01:05:11.883 --> 01:05:14.159
I don't want these YouTube
idiots on my network.

01:05:14.159 --> 01:05:16.595
For whatever reason, for
hangups that they have

01:05:16.595 --> 01:05:18.551
or they just, like you
said, they don't like us.

01:05:18.551 --> 01:05:19.586
They don't like our sense of humor.

01:05:19.586 --> 01:05:20.617
It's stupid, whatever.

01:05:20.617 --> 01:05:22.258
They don't like the
fact that you're picky.

01:05:22.258 --> 01:05:23.649
They don't like the fact
that we're not chefs.

01:05:23.649 --> 01:05:26.209
Feeling that they don't
like my hair, whatever.

01:05:26.209 --> 01:05:30.226
I already know that there's
people who think that.

01:05:30.226 --> 01:05:31.175
I already know that there are people

01:05:31.175 --> 01:05:32.316
who think we're insufferable.

01:05:32.316 --> 01:05:33.941
Do I need to hear them say it?

01:05:33.941 --> 01:05:36.607
So.
We also don't need them

01:05:36.607 --> 01:05:37.782
to change their mind.

01:05:37.782 --> 01:05:40.388
Right.
We're doing just fine.

01:05:40.388 --> 01:05:44.438
Yeah and so that's what
I'm saying ultimately is,

01:05:44.438 --> 01:05:45.404
I don't think.

01:05:45.404 --> 01:05:48.839
I'm definitely not gonna
seek out any sort of,

01:05:48.839 --> 01:05:51.683
I heard somebody saying one time,

01:05:51.683 --> 01:05:53.311
"Never read your book review.

01:05:53.311 --> 01:05:54.620
"Never read your movie review."

01:05:54.620 --> 01:05:55.570
If we ever have the privilege

01:05:55.570 --> 01:05:58.320
of making a feature-length movie,

01:05:59.767 --> 01:06:02.355
I don't think I'm gonna
read any critic reviews.

01:06:02.355 --> 01:06:03.304
Whoa.
I don't think

01:06:03.304 --> 01:06:04.252
I'm gonna go to Rotten Tomatoes.

01:06:04.252 --> 01:06:05.776
Now I'm gonna know what
the aggregate score is

01:06:05.776 --> 01:06:08.144
because you can't avoid it
and somebody's gonna tell us.

01:06:08.144 --> 01:06:10.646
It's gonna be in some report
that comes in an email.

01:06:10.646 --> 01:06:13.121
Everyone, your movie exists.

01:06:13.121 --> 01:06:14.541
It is currently at a 61.

