01:07:05.926 --> 01:07:06.841
The things that really hurt

01:07:06.841 --> 01:07:08.715
are the things where
we know it's a weakness

01:07:08.715 --> 01:07:10.028
and we wish we could've changed it.

01:07:10.028 --> 01:07:11.846
Like that's when it really
gets me is that like.

01:07:11.846 --> 01:07:12.910
Yeah, but I think there's.

01:07:12.910 --> 01:07:13.810
But I guess what I'm

01:07:13.810 --> 01:07:14.709
saying ultimately.
There are some

01:07:14.709 --> 01:07:15.931
of those things but those are small.

01:07:15.931 --> 01:07:17.984
When it comes to these four episodes,

01:07:17.984 --> 01:07:20.901
there's not any gaping shortcoming.

01:07:22.116 --> 01:07:22.994
Yeah, yeah I agree.

01:07:22.994 --> 01:07:24.462
That I feel is like a big weakness.

01:07:24.462 --> 01:07:25.336
It is what it is.
I agree with that.

01:07:25.336 --> 01:07:26.590
I mean it's not, you know again it's not.

01:07:26.590 --> 01:07:28.007
I mean we're not.

01:07:29.189 --> 01:07:31.356
I was, honestly it's like,

01:07:32.843 --> 01:07:34.257
are we trying to win an Emmy?

01:07:34.257 --> 01:07:35.225
No.

01:07:35.225 --> 01:07:36.119
No, of course not.

01:07:36.119 --> 01:07:37.780
I mean maybe eventually

01:07:37.780 --> 01:07:39.005
but we don't think that this show is

01:07:39.005 --> 01:07:40.056
gonna do that.
No it's like,

01:07:40.056 --> 01:07:42.052
I mean some of my favorite shows ever,

01:07:42.052 --> 01:07:43.854
I don't know if they ever won an Emmy.

01:07:43.854 --> 01:07:45.008
Right.
Did Dirty Jobs

01:07:45.008 --> 01:07:45.882
ever win an Emmy?

01:07:45.882 --> 01:07:48.145
Yeah so.
Maybe, I don't know.

01:07:48.145 --> 01:07:49.876
I think it deserves one.

01:07:49.876 --> 01:07:51.395
I completely agree with you

01:07:51.395 --> 01:07:55.773
that the stuff that I
already know to be true.

01:07:55.773 --> 01:07:59.023
It's like this person thinks this thing

01:08:00.297 --> 01:08:01.909
and they perceive us in this way.

01:08:01.909 --> 01:08:03.697
That's not the stuff that bothers me.

01:08:03.697 --> 01:08:04.918
The stuff that bothers me

01:08:04.918 --> 01:08:08.835
is the stuff that I
already know to be the case

01:08:09.682 --> 01:08:12.484
that's like yes, we made this mistake

01:08:12.484 --> 01:08:13.960
or we did this thing wrong

01:08:13.960 --> 01:08:16.565
and now people are
basically recognizing that

01:08:16.565 --> 01:08:18.810
and my worst fear of people finding out

01:08:18.810 --> 01:08:21.426
that we made this mistake and
did this in the wrong way.

01:08:21.426 --> 01:08:22.962
It's coming true.
Right.

01:08:22.962 --> 01:08:25.453
What I'm saying is from
an emotional standpoint,

01:08:25.453 --> 01:08:29.097
I already know the
mistakes that I've made.

01:08:29.097 --> 01:08:30.269
And I'm not talking about with this.

01:08:30.269 --> 01:08:31.455
I agree with you.

01:08:31.455 --> 01:08:33.173
I don't feel that way about this show.

01:08:33.173 --> 01:08:34.164
I'm just saying in general,

01:08:34.164 --> 01:08:35.864
with the things that
we put into the world.

01:08:35.864 --> 01:08:38.172
I have just found that
I'm in a healthier place

01:08:38.172 --> 01:08:40.696
when I'm like you know what was lacking

01:08:40.696 --> 01:08:42.052
about that thing that you did.

01:08:42.052 --> 01:08:45.314
Do you need somebody to tell
you when you already know?

01:08:45.314 --> 01:08:47.315
And do you gain anything
emotionally from it?

01:08:47.315 --> 01:08:52.315
So if I can have somebody
else read all that feedback

01:08:52.430 --> 01:08:53.717
and then come to us and be like,

01:08:53.717 --> 01:08:56.735
"Hey this is actually
how things were received

01:08:56.735 --> 01:08:58.485
"from a whole group."

01:08:59.575 --> 01:09:02.611
That's much less emotionally unsettling

01:09:02.611 --> 01:09:05.839
than reading individual people
say very personal things.

01:09:05.839 --> 01:09:09.870
So I'm not saying I can't deal with it.

01:09:09.870 --> 01:09:13.246
I'm just saying after it
happens, I think to myself,

01:09:13.246 --> 01:09:14.746
"I could have not.

01:09:15.902 --> 01:09:17.756
"I could have not experienced that

01:09:17.756 --> 01:09:19.762
"and I would be having
a better time right now.

01:09:19.762 --> 01:09:21.360
"I would be in a healthier place."

01:09:21.360 --> 01:09:22.693
Yeah I get it.

01:09:23.570 --> 01:09:26.070
This is not a GMM 22 scenario.

01:09:27.183 --> 01:09:28.720
Oh.
I mean you know that.

01:09:28.720 --> 01:09:30.847
Of course.
I think that's my point.

01:09:30.847 --> 01:09:32.111
Yeah.
You know it's like,

01:09:32.111 --> 01:09:35.287
we did that First We Feast snacked video

01:09:35.287 --> 01:09:39.327
and I read those comments and
you get the people who don't,

01:09:39.327 --> 01:09:40.447
they're not fans of ours.

01:09:40.447 --> 01:09:42.991
Who maybe don't have a point
of reference for us and yeah,

01:09:42.991 --> 01:09:45.599
I do remember the comment
about me that was like,

01:09:45.599 --> 01:09:49.016
"This guy just, he like, he acts and eats

01:09:50.194 --> 01:09:51.801
"like a four-year-old."

01:09:51.801 --> 01:09:53.551
It's like okay, well.

01:09:55.755 --> 01:09:56.838
That's, he's,

01:09:58.265 --> 01:10:00.452
this commenter's describing something.

01:10:00.452 --> 01:10:03.410
That could've hurt my
feelings but the thing I'm,

01:10:03.410 --> 01:10:06.449
the way I'm trying to
grow is to interact with,

01:10:06.449 --> 01:10:07.754
not interact with the comment.

01:10:07.754 --> 01:10:11.454
But to acknowledge the
comment within myself as,

01:10:11.454 --> 01:10:12.310
"You know what?

01:10:12.310 --> 01:10:16.338
"He's describing something
that people are attracted to

01:10:16.338 --> 01:10:19.005
"about my sense of humor and my persona."

01:10:19.005 --> 01:10:22.120
Yeah.
That he doesn't get.

01:10:22.120 --> 01:10:24.134
Or doesn't prefer.

01:10:24.134 --> 01:10:25.285
And it's not for everybody.
And you know what?

01:10:25.285 --> 01:10:28.035
So I mean, but I was fully myself

01:10:30.149 --> 01:10:31.701
and I'm very proud of it

01:10:31.701 --> 01:10:33.577
and I don't expect everybody to like me

01:10:33.577 --> 01:10:34.673
and I'm cool with that.

01:10:34.673 --> 01:10:35.651
And I actually remember thinking.

01:10:35.651 --> 01:10:36.678
Just trying to be cool with that.

01:10:36.678 --> 01:10:37.511
That's a good example

01:10:37.511 --> 01:10:39.275
because I remember
thinking that when we left

01:10:39.275 --> 01:10:41.716
that First We Feast shoot.

01:10:41.716 --> 01:10:43.745
That I was like a four-year-old?

01:10:43.745 --> 01:10:44.885
Yeah.

01:10:44.885 --> 01:10:46.448
I remember thinking,

01:10:46.448 --> 01:10:48.908
we were really ourselves

01:10:48.908 --> 01:10:51.815
and we were having a genuinely good time

01:10:51.815 --> 01:10:54.009
just being ourselves and
interacting with these snacks

01:10:54.009 --> 01:10:56.509
and I am proud of what we did.

01:10:57.394 --> 01:10:58.386
The only thing I was pissed about

01:10:58.386 --> 01:11:01.469
was they didn't buy the right cereal.

01:11:02.483 --> 01:11:04.851
So that's why there was
no cereal in the episode

01:11:04.851 --> 01:11:06.934
and they also cut your beans.
They edited it out.

01:11:06.934 --> 01:11:09.275
I did have baked beans
and that was edited out.

01:11:09.275 --> 01:11:10.108
So just for the record,

01:11:10.108 --> 01:11:12.336
Rhett ate beans and I ordered cereal

01:11:12.336 --> 01:11:16.572
but Raisin Bran is not Raisin
Bran Crunch and that's not.

01:11:16.572 --> 01:11:20.822
And by the way, Raisin Bran
is not Raisin Nut Bran.

01:11:23.248 --> 01:11:24.172
Okay.

01:11:24.172 --> 01:11:26.752
And that's the one I actually ordered

01:11:26.752 --> 01:11:28.128
'cause I'm on that kick now.

01:11:28.128 --> 01:11:28.982
Raisin Nut Bran Crunch?

01:11:28.982 --> 01:11:29.815
Nope.
Or just Raisin Nut Bran?

01:11:29.815 --> 01:11:30.648
Raisin Nut Bran.

01:11:30.648 --> 01:11:32.017
Not Raisin Bran Crunch.

01:11:32.017 --> 01:11:34.697
But so.
And I was pissed about that

01:11:34.697 --> 01:11:36.566
but you know, mistakes are made and.

01:11:36.566 --> 01:11:38.364
And I knew when we came as a duo.

01:11:38.364 --> 01:11:39.612
It really isn't a big deal.

01:11:39.612 --> 01:11:41.700
When we came as a duo and
we had all those snacks,

01:11:41.700 --> 01:11:43.889
I knew that something
was gonna be cut out.

01:11:43.889 --> 01:11:46.139
But what I'm getting at is,

01:11:47.197 --> 01:11:49.264
even though I did, when it came out.

01:11:49.264 --> 01:11:50.944
I did start scrolling
through the comments.

01:11:50.944 --> 01:11:53.022
I stopped because I was like,

01:11:53.022 --> 01:11:55.304
"Hold on, you remember
walking out of there

01:11:55.304 --> 01:11:56.594
"and thinking to yourself,

01:11:56.594 --> 01:11:59.605
"'You did that the way
that you wanted to do it.'"

01:11:59.605 --> 01:12:01.775
Now any time you venture outside

01:12:01.775 --> 01:12:03.693
of your protective bubble of your.

01:12:03.693 --> 01:12:06.071
Mythical Beast.
Your Mythical Beasts.

01:12:06.071 --> 01:12:09.375
You know that you're ready for,

01:12:09.375 --> 01:12:10.832
you're gonna get some criticism.

01:12:10.832 --> 01:12:12.527
And so again, I was like,

01:12:12.527 --> 01:12:14.107
yes people aren't gonna like it.

01:12:14.107 --> 01:12:17.213
Some people just look at us
and are immediately annoyed.

01:12:17.213 --> 01:12:19.537
I understand, I get it.

01:12:19.537 --> 01:12:21.569
I know people like that too.

01:12:21.569 --> 01:12:24.314
Right.
But if I'm happy

01:12:24.314 --> 01:12:26.386
with what I did and how I came across,

01:12:26.386 --> 01:12:29.146
then I should just let that be

01:12:29.146 --> 01:12:30.717
what I found the satisfaction in.

01:12:30.717 --> 01:12:32.970
Not that somebody liked
it or didn't like it.

01:12:32.970 --> 01:12:34.428
Again 'cause I don't want to just

01:12:34.428 --> 01:12:36.277
hear things that people like either.

01:12:36.277 --> 01:12:39.533
I'm saying that finding any sort of value

01:12:39.533 --> 01:12:44.533
or currency in people liking
me or feeling undervalued

01:12:44.635 --> 01:12:46.567
because people don't like me.

01:12:46.567 --> 01:12:49.520
I'm just trying to move to
a new level of existence

01:12:49.520 --> 01:12:51.546
and it's really difficult for a performer

01:12:51.546 --> 01:12:52.640
who has built a career.
Oh yeah.

01:12:52.640 --> 01:12:54.235
On trying to please an audience.

01:12:54.235 --> 01:12:57.646
It's just part of the ongoing struggle.

01:12:57.646 --> 01:13:00.337
So when we've got something
like this, that's again.

01:13:00.337 --> 01:13:03.651
I don't know how many people
are going to watch the show

01:13:03.651 --> 01:13:06.074
compared to how many people
watch Good Mythical Morning.

01:13:06.074 --> 01:13:08.907
I think less given how many people

01:13:09.744 --> 01:13:11.174
watch Good Mythical Morning.

01:13:11.174 --> 01:13:15.038
But it's still going to be
perceived as some leveling up.

01:13:15.038 --> 01:13:16.772
It's like the people back
home in North Carolina,

01:13:16.772 --> 01:13:18.529
oh they're all excited about the TV show

01:13:18.529 --> 01:13:20.500
because it means more to them.

01:13:20.500 --> 01:13:22.179
Because they think that
being on television

01:13:22.179 --> 01:13:23.647
instead of having a YouTube show

01:13:23.647 --> 01:13:27.545
is like a fundamentally
different, more awesome thing.

01:13:27.545 --> 01:13:29.432
It's just how people think about things.

01:13:29.432 --> 01:13:33.849
So you feel like you're
stepping up onto some sort of

01:13:36.273 --> 01:13:38.974
pseudo-pedestal and now
people are gonna be like,

01:13:38.974 --> 01:13:39.972
"Well now that they've done this,

01:13:39.972 --> 01:13:41.744
"now I've gotta have my opinion."

01:13:41.744 --> 01:13:42.577
And I'm just like,

01:13:42.577 --> 01:13:43.873
"Well I already know what
I think about what we did.

01:13:43.873 --> 01:13:45.785
"I already know about the show.

01:13:45.785 --> 01:13:48.388
"So I should not even hear your opinion."

01:13:48.388 --> 01:13:49.737
Does that make sense?

01:13:49.737 --> 01:13:50.570
Yeah.

